snake plant (sansevieria) - the tall one by the bookshelf

- the easiest plant I own. almost impossible to kill except by drowning it.
- soak the pot thoroughly, then let the soil dry out completely before the next time. in practice: every 14 days or so in summer, once a month in winter.
- stick a finger 5 cm into the soil; if there is any dampness, wait.
- indirect light is ideal but it tolerated the dark corner for a year.
- yellow soft leaves at the base = too much. cut them off and wait longer.
- repot only when the roots crack the pot. it likes being crowded.
